IO-62: label the inlet count column in the SI Street Flow Summary

writeStreetStatsHeader() writes "Count" over the inlet count column for US
units but leaves it blank in the SI version of the same header line. Add the
label; the line keeps its length, so no column moves.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-62_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
index fa52cb3..9fcc637 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/inlet.c
@@ -1044,7 +1044,7 @@ void writeStreetStatsHeader()
 "\n  Street Conduit         %3s        ft        ft  Design            Location  Count     Pcnt     Pcnt     Pcnt     Pcnt      %3s      %3s",
         FlowUnitWords[FlowUnits], FlowUnitWords[FlowUnits], FlowUnitWords[FlowUnits]);
     else fprintf(Frpt.file,
-"\n  Street Conduit         %3s         m         m  Design            Location            Pcnt     Pcnt     Pcnt     Pcnt      %3s      %3s",
+"\n  Street Conduit         %3s         m         m  Design            Location  Count     Pcnt     Pcnt     Pcnt     Pcnt      %3s      %3s",
         FlowUnitWords[FlowUnits], FlowUnitWords[FlowUnits], FlowUnitWords[FlowUnits]);
     fprintf(Frpt.file,
 "\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------");
